Year-over-Year Monthly Sales Analysis

Business Question
How did monthly sales performance evolve in 2017 compared to the previous year?

Methodology
Monthly sales were aggregated using time-series resampling. A year-over-year comparison was created by shifting monthly sales values by 12 months to align equivalent reporting periods.
This approach enables trend comparison, seasonality analysis, and identification of performance deviations across time.

(transactions
 .set_index("date")
 .sort_index() 
 .loc[:, ["SALES_VALUE"]] 
 .resample("ME")
 .sum()
 .assign(year_prior= lambda x: x["SALES_VALUE"].shift(12))
 .loc["2017"]
 .plot()
)



Key Insight
Monthly sales in 2017 show a generally stable performance pattern across most of the year. From April to November, sales remained relatively consistent compared to prior-year levels, with an average year-over-year deviation of approximately 28,000 in monthly sales.
Higher volatility is observed in early-year and year-end periods, indicating seasonal fluctuations and temporary deviations in demand patterns.

